2026-05-15  Kamila Szewczyk  <k@iczelia.net>

	v1.0:  Initial release of fastent.

	Tests: Shannon entropy, chi-square (with tail probability),
	arithmetic mean, Monte Carlo Pi, serial correlation.  Byte
	mode by default; bit mode under -b.  In-line case fold under
	-f, fused into the SIMD body.

	Outputs: human-readable text, CSV (-t), JSON (--json), with
	an optional per-value occurrences table (-c) and full
	precision rendering (-p).

	Throughput: 4-way banked SIMD histogram, sign-corrected
	PMADDUBSW serial-correlation cross-product, VPOPCNTB
	bit-mode popcount on AVX-512 BITALG hosts with a PSHUFB
	nibble lookup fallback, runtime CPUID dispatch across
	scalar / SSSE3 / SSE4.1 / AVX2 / AVX-512.  Memory-mapped
	input with MADV_SEQUENTIAL on regular files, 2 MiB read(2)
	loop otherwise.

	Threading: optional pthread worker pool (-j N / --threads),
	6-aligned slab partitioning, deterministic byte-identical
	merge.  -j auto resolves to one thread per online CPU.

	Platforms: Linux musl (x86_64, i386, aarch64, armhf,
	riscv64, ppc64le, ppc64, ppc, s390x, loongarch64, mips,
	mipsel, mips64, mips64el), Linux glibc (alpha, sparc64,
	sparc, m68k, hppa, arc, sh4), Windows (x86_64, i686,
	aarch64), Windows 95 (i686, kernel32+msvcrt only), macOS
	(x86_64, aarch64), MS-DOS via DJGPP with CWSDPMI bundled.

	Build: GNU autotools.  --enable-native, --enable-lto,
	--disable-threads, --with-windows-target=vista|win95.

	Testing: deterministic-fixture suite under make check,
	throughput benchmark sweep under make bench.
